.TH MKNOD 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mknod \- creates a filesystem node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.B int mknod(const char* path, mode_t mode, unsigned int device);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a filesystem node. device is the raw Linux kernel-encoded 32-bit device number, not a libc dev_t; regular files and FIFOs use zero. Permissions and capabilities apply.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mknod (2)
